## Why This Is Asked
This explores cost-aware telemetry and basic privacy controls in a common API stack.

## Key Concepts
- Deterministic per-tenant sampling
- Privacy: IP redaction
- Streaming: SDK -> Pub/Sub
- Storage: Parquet/BigQuery regional
- Testing: volume control, privacy, dashboard freshness

## Code Example
```javascript
function shouldSample(tenantId, eventId, rate) {
  const seed = `${tenantId}-${eventId}`;
  let h = 0;
  for (let i = 0; i < seed.length; i++) h = (h * 31 + seed.charCodeAt(i)) >>> 0;
  return (h % 100) < rate;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you handle dynamic rate changes per tenant at runtime?
- What if a tenant exceeds their quota; how would you implement backpressure?

## Why This Is Asked

Assess ability to enforce data quality at ingestion in a beginner OTCA setting, with per-tenant controls and end-to-end lifecycle.

## Key Concepts

- Ingest-time validation and whitelist
- Idempotency and dedup
- Per-tenant partitioning in storage
- Auditability of dropped records

## Code Example

```javascript
function validate(event, knownTenants){
  if(!event.tenant_id || !knownTenants.includes(event.tenant_id)) return false;
  if(!['login','click','error','latency'].includes(event.event_type)) return false;
  const ts = new Date(event.timestamp);
  const now = new Date();
  if(isNaN(ts) || Math.abs(now - ts) > 7*24*60*60*1000) return false;
  if(event.latency_ms != null && event.latency_ms < 0) return false;
  return true;
}
``` 

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you handle schema evolution at ingestion without breaking existing pipelines?
- How would you implement a lightweight audit log for dropped events and partial successes?
